<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  LegacyEcommerce.edmx : EF6 Database First visual model (DRAFT / PENDING SYNC).

  STATUS: checked in BEFORE the database has been created. The SQL script
  database\01_Create_LegacyEcommerceDb.sql must be reviewed and executed with
  explicit approval first. Until then this EDMX MUST NOT be treated as
  synchronized with any live database.

  AFTER the database exists, open this file in Visual Studio and run
  "Update Model from Database..." to regenerate it from LegacyEcommerceDb on
  .\SQLEXPRESS, then rebuild.

  Runtime note: EcommerceDbContext (EcommerceDbContext.cs, same folder) carries
  a code-first mapping that mirrors the reviewed SQL script table-for-table, so
  the application builds and runs against the script schema whether or not this
  EDMX has been re-synced. Build Action is None on purpose: design-time only.

  ASP.NET Identity tables (AspNetUsers / AspNetRoles / ...) are intentionally
  NOT part of this model; they are owned by the Identity context in
  Ecommerce.Web (see Models\IdentityModels.cs).
-->
